(783371, 86226, 11738, '<td valign="top">Your outside.  Challenge clearly sated that you had to be indoors.  Also, the tree''s sahdow fooled your camera and the shot is slightly overexposed.<br/> <br/>The angle used to shoot your subject is too perpendicular to your subjects.  A suggestion if you would like to shoot this again: use a low angle shot (shoot from on your knees,  looking up) in front of the horse and just capture the horse''s head , bridal (sp?), part of te reins and the rider from waist up.  Another idea would have been a waist-up shot of the rider standing on the ground with both horse and rider looking (or not) at the camera.  Both these shots would permit you to get closer to your subjects and put more emphasis on facial features.</td>', 'Your outside.  Challenge clearly sated that you had to be indoors.  Also, the tree''s sahdow fooled your camera and the shot is slightly overexposed. The angle used to shoot your subject is too perpendicular to your subjects.  A suggestion if you would like to shoot this again: use a low angle shot (shoot from on your knees,  looking up) in front of the horse and just capture the horse''s head , bridal (sp?), part of te reins and the rider from waist up.  Another idea would have been a waist-up shot of the rider standing on the ground with both horse and rider looking (or not) at the camera.  Both these shots would permit you to get closer to your subjects and put more emphasis on facial features.', '2004-06-28 17:54:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(783372, 86075, 18080, '<td valign="top">Good skin tones and nice slice of life picture. Background is a bit too "white" for this to make a good shot in my opinion.<br/>Good luck though</td>', 'Good skin tones and nice slice of life picture. Background is a bit too "white" for this to make a good shot in my opinion.Good luck though', '2004-06-28 17:54:32.000000', NULL, 1),
