INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(787508, 85855, 8860, '<td valign="top">... you will find me!  :D<br/> <br/>Mischievous expression (that''s what I''ve read into it anyway!!) and beautiful natural lighting. She''s a bit low in the frame though and a bit more definition in her hair would be good. She certainly must have some incredibly good looking parents...  ;)</td>', '... you will find me!  :D Mischievous expression (that''s what I''ve read into it anyway!!) and beautiful natural lighting. She''s a bit low in the frame though and a bit more definition in her hair would be good. She certainly must have some incredibly good looking parents...  ;)', '2004-06-30 15:59:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(787509, 86089, 8860, '<td valign="top">Lovely shot of the bride and her baby son!!  :D<br/> <br/>Seriously though, I love the colour of this. The high-key works well and the composition is great. I must say though that the pose is almost comical, so if he were placed just slightly higher then it may work even better and look less like a Freudian visage!<br/> <br/>But - boy is that title going to p**s you off over time!!</td>', 'Lovely shot of the bride and her baby son!!  :D Seriously though, I love the colour of this. The high-key works well and the composition is great. I must say though that the pose is almost comical, so if he were placed just slightly higher then it may work even better and look less like a Freudian visage! But - boy is that title going to p**s you off over time!!', '2004-06-30 16:00:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(787510, 85780, 16004, '<td valign="top">this has the appearance of being let down slightly be the over-use of neat-image or some such.  a grainy shot is probably preferable, to be honest...   i''m only guessing, but it would be that you also blurred the background - this is seemingly apparent from whats left around the ears and side of face.  third and final point is that the lighting seems harsh - i''m completely no expert, but it might help if your model didn''t look into the light source, becuase it makes the eyes contract and appear not quite natural.  the pose and ocmposition is very good though, and cropping out half the hat is a good move (it''s weird how many would want all the hat in the shot).</td>', 'this has the appearance of being let down slightly be the over-use of neat-image or some such.  a grainy shot is probably preferable, to be honest...   i''m only guessing, but it would be that you also blurred the background - this is seemingly apparent from whats left around the ears and side of face.  third and final point is that the lighting seems harsh - i''m completely no expert, but it might help if your model didn''t look into the light source, becuase it makes the eyes contract and appear not quite natural.  the pose and ocmposition is very good though, and cropping out half the hat is a good move (it''s weird how many would want all the hat in the shot).', '2004-06-30 16:00:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(787514, 86120, 16004, '<td valign="top">i''m a little in two minds over this.  i love how white everything is, and i think it''s a very beautiful image.  with regards to its portraitedness, i''m not entirely sure...  traditionally, the face shouldn''t be obscured, but it has so much style and drama, i don''t really mind.   i bit more colour in the eyes would be nice though, and possibly a little cloning in her right eye, because the reflections look a bit messy.  nice shot though - 7.</td>', 'i''m a little in two minds over this.  i love how white everything is, and i think it''s a very beautiful image.  with regards to its portraitedness, i''m not entirely sure...  traditionally, the face shouldn''t be obscured, but it has so much style and drama, i don''t really mind.   i bit more colour in the eyes would be nice though, and possibly a little cloning in her right eye, because the reflections look a bit messy.  nice shot though - 7.', '2004-06-30 16:03:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(787515, 86315, 20375, '<td valign="top">Good job. My criticism is hard to explain...but this pretty lady has her chin<br/>sort of tucked in I think because she has tilted it to one side. <br/>Still, nice job the hair and the background match perfectly.</td>', 'Good job. My criticism is hard to explain...but this pretty lady has her chinsort of tucked in I think because she has tilted it to one side. Still, nice job the hair and the background match perfectly.', '2004-06-30 16:06:06.000000', NULL, 1),
