(795942, 85855, 4090, '<td valign="top">Nice photo Gordon, Lighting is great - IMHO if it was sharper maybe a high score but a lady portrait needs to be a bit soft.. If you know what I mean.. Plus your lucky have someone to pose for you, I''m Not allowed to point my camera at Suzie (the wee wife) Regards Tony</td>', 'Nice photo Gordon, Lighting is great - IMHO if it was sharper maybe a high score but a lady portrait needs to be a bit soft.. If you know what I mean.. Plus your lucky have someone to pose for you, I''m Not allowed to point my camera at Suzie (the wee wife) Regards Tony', '2004-07-05 04:17:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(795945, 85693, 16188, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the comments - I learn from them all.  I think this image worked pretty well because it illicited a lot of thoughtful comments and some responses along the lines of what I was trying to accomplish (even some of the criticisms fit in that category since they validate that my goals were met albeit in a backhanded kind of way).  One thing I realized reading the comments here was that I sometimes do things for effect which don''t work.  In this case, it was the glitter in the left eye.  I left that in on purpose because, at a larger size, you can see a reflection of my back garden through the window and that intrigued me.  At this size, however, it is just distracting.  I appreciate it when people take the time to comment and these have all been thoughtful.  Thanks to everyone who left comments and thanks to whoever gave me those  9''s and 10''s! :)<br/></td>', 'Thanks for all the comments - I learn from them all.  I think this image worked pretty well because it illicited a lot of thoughtful comments and some responses along the lines of what I was trying to accomplish (even some of the criticisms fit in that category since they validate that my goals were met albeit in a backhanded kind of way).  One thing I realized reading the comments here was that I sometimes do things for effect which don''t work.  In this case, it was the glitter in the left eye.  I left that in on purpose because, at a larger size, you can see a reflection of my back garden through the window and that intrigued me.  At this size, however, it is just distracting.  I appreciate it when people take the time to comment and these have all been thoughtful.  Thanks to everyone who left comments and thanks to whoever gave me those  9''s and 10''s! :)', '2004-07-05 04:19:38.000000', NULL, 0),
