(796000, 86163, 15832, '<td valign="top">Color portrait not colorful portrait.....<br/>I was trying to make a colorful portrait. So i made this huge colorpot;)<br/>Then i see that mine is the only one so colorful.. And the others portrait... Are just in color.. ;Þ<br/> <br/>Thanks for all the comment..<br/>Alot of useful information.</td>', 'Color portrait not colorful portrait.....I was trying to make a colorful portrait. So i made this huge colorpot;)Then i see that mine is the only one so colorful.. And the others portrait... Are just in color.. ;Þ Thanks for all the comment..Alot of useful information.', '2004-07-05 06:36:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(796001, 85855, 14603, '<td valign="top">Thanks to all for the comments..I have learned a lot from this challenge ..mostly that my daughter is worth a few points of a start for me as a model..so I`ll have to keep her sweet   :-)<br/> <br/>Paul..your right..there`s not a lot this camera (and a bit of luck) can`t do..I`ve been considering upgrading and then think..why ?<br/> <br/>Manny...a 9 from the MASTER of portraiture..I am genuinely chuffed to think I`ve improved that much from my last attempt.<br/>I had your submission marked as a definite ribbon winner.<br/>Incidentally, I haven`t submitted to the "Purple" challenge..but you`ve got me intrigued..I`ll have to look through them.<br/> <br/>Tony,thanks for the comments, I did wonder which way to go but decided to plump for softening the image..My daughter is actually sitting at the dining table near the lounge window..the background was cream wallpaper which I had to darken.leaving the halo around some parts of the image..quite a studio set-up..eh<br/>My wife refuses to pose either after the last portrait disaster.<br/> <br/>Regards<br/>Gordon</td>', 'Thanks to all for the comments..I have learned a lot from this challenge ..mostly that my daughter is worth a few points of a start for me as a model..so I`ll have to keep her sweet   :-) Paul..your right..there`s not a lot this camera (and a bit of luck) can`t do..I`ve been considering upgrading and then think..why ? Manny...a 9 from the MASTER of portraiture..I am genuinely chuffed to think I`ve improved that much from my last attempt.I had your submission marked as a definite ribbon winner.Incidentally, I haven`t submitted to the "Purple" challenge..but you`ve got me intrigued..I`ll have to look through them. Tony,thanks for the comments, I did wonder which way to go but decided to plump for softening the image..My daughter is actually sitting at the dining table near the lounge window..the background was cream wallpaper which I had to darken.leaving the halo around some parts of the image..quite a studio set-up..ehMy wife refuses to pose either after the last portrait disaster. RegardsGordon', '2004-07-05 06:37:02.000000', NULL, 0),
