(796855, 85816, 18897, '<td valign="top">Missed the voting on this challenge, but post-browsing through the entries your image really stands out and I''m pretty confident that you would have gotten my single 10 vote for this round. It wouldn''t have made much of a difference for you in the end, but you deserve the recognition now that I found it.<br/> <br/>Very nice with ppl who dare interpret the challenges a bit different without getting astray from the subject too much. I agree with those who deem it fit.<br/> <br/>Amazing use of the light!</td>', 'Missed the voting on this challenge, but post-browsing through the entries your image really stands out and I''m pretty confident that you would have gotten my single 10 vote for this round. It wouldn''t have made much of a difference for you in the end, but you deserve the recognition now that I found it. Very nice with ppl who dare interpret the challenges a bit different without getting astray from the subject too much. I agree with those who deem it fit. Amazing use of the light!', '2004-07-05 18:09:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(796868, 85938, 7151, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by soup:</b></div><hr/><i> i am against the majority with this one, and would say that it lacks emotion due to the lack of a background.  it looks set up, and over processed. - congrats none-the-less </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Repeat after me:  Color Studio Portrait.  Color <b>Studio</b> Portrait.<br/>Of course it looks set up - its a Color <b>STUDIO</b> Portrait.<br/> <br/>Great work Sonifo.  This was my top pick for the challenge.  The perfect balance of studio control and candid, non-posed subject.  (I was pretty sure this was yours when during voting - it has your touch all over it.)</td>', 'Originally posted by soup: i am against the majority with this one, and would say that it lacks emotion due to the lack of a background.  it looks set up, and over processed. - congrats none-the-less   Repeat after me:  Color Studio Portrait.  Color Studio Portrait.Of course it looks set up - its a Color STUDIO Portrait. Great work Sonifo.  This was my top pick for the challenge.  The perfect balance of studio control and candid, non-posed subject.  (I was pretty sure this was yours when during voting - it has your touch all over it.)', '2004-07-05 18:31:22.000000', NULL, 0),
